statement:
Let $f$ be a function defined on the set of non-negative integers and taking values in the same set. Given that
\begin{enumerate}
\item[(a)] $x - f(x) = 19\left\lfloor \d\frac{x}{19} \right\rfloor - 90\left\lfloor \d\frac{f(x)}{90} \right\rfloor$ for all non-negative integers $x$;
\item[(b)] $1900 < f(1990) < 2000$,
\end{enumerate}
find the possible values that $f(1990)$ can take.
